===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wikipedia|noggin (protein)}}

# A [[small]] [[mug]], [[cup]] or [[ladle]]; the contents of such a container.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1889|author=[[w:Arthur Conan Doyle|Arthur Conan Doyle]]|title=[[s:The Parson of Jackman's Gulch]]
|passage=Here Nat Adams, the burly bar-keeper, dispensed bad whisky at the rate of two shillings a '''noggin''', or a guinea a bottle…}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1999|artist=Dervish|artistlink=Dervish|album=Midsummer's Night|title=Bold Doherty|url=https://genius.com/Dervish-bold-doherty-song-lyrics|passage=I needed some nails for to rivet them down...When you go to town you can buy the full '''noggin''' but beware you bring none of your fancibles home.}} 
# {{lb|en|dated|outside|dialects}} A small measure of [[spirits]] equivalent to a [[gill]].
#* {{RQ:Dickens Pickwick Papers|chapter=49|passage=I don’t know whether any of you, gentlemen, ever partook of a real, substantial, hospitable Scotch breakfast, and then went to a slight lunch of a bushel of oysters, a dozen or so of bottled ale, and a '''noggin''' or two of whisky to close up with.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} The [[head]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=James D. Doss|title=Dead Soul|url=http://books.google.com/books?vid=ISBN0312317441&id=LYVtbyi2BFEC&pg=PA136&lpg=PA136&ots=caRgQRq-7E&dq=%22bumped+his+noggin%22&sig=q5kBJVoKK15FwmN_EhcNVQeTPV4
|passage=Or maybe he bumped his '''noggin''' when he fell down—after he got clipped on the legs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=John Farris|title=The Fury and the Power|url=http://books.google.com/books?vid=ISBN0312877285&id=YNLXjR-BKSQC&pg=PA119&lpg=PA119&ots=Bz5V2NIwpI&dq=%22bumped+her+noggin%22&sig=iYyYDUozgqkUxVL0dFJVLrZubvc
|passage=She bumped her '''noggin''' on the bulkhead above the doorway, smiled in apology for her presumed clumsiness.}}
# {{lb|en|biochemistry}} A [[signal]]ling [[molecule]] involved in [[embryo]] [[development]], producing large [[head]]s at high [[concentration]]s.
# {{alt form|en|nogging|gloss=horizontal beam}}

